From 179ebd55a141c24bcc166c2e9d538bc5303d56b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:52:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Make the scan log collapsible with the filter always in
 the header

The scan log table (up to 40 rows, now with a Factors column too) was
always fully rendered on the dashboard, pushing everything below it
down the page even when nobody was reading it.

- Added a Show/Hide button to the scan log header. The table (and the
  "showing: X" filter status line) now lives in a collapsed panel by
  default and only renders open when you actually want to look at it.
- The symbol filter box and Filter/Clear buttons stay in the header
  itself, so you can filter without first expanding the table - and
  submitting a filter opens the panel automatically since you clearly
  want to see the result.
- Auto-refresh (every 45s) now also pauses while the log panel is
  open, same as it already did for an expanded signal row, so a
  reload doesn't yank the table shut while you're reading it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TTwCHXT3HSQFTa3kX6yUDc
---
 templates/index.html | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/templates/index.html b/templates/index.html
